# Visual iteration

The globe is a WebGL canvas. You cannot see it until you capture a PNG.

After any change that affects how the planet looks (shaders, colors, terrain, rivers, plates, camera, mesh, colormap):

1. Run `bun run preview`
2. Read `preview/compare.png` if it exists (before | after). Otherwise read `preview/planet.png`.
3. Judge the image, then change the code and repeat

Do not finish visual work from code alone. Each globe is a 2x2 of four longitudes: 0, 90, 180, and 270 degrees. `preview/planet.png` is always the latest capture; older ones are in `preview/planet-before.png` and `preview/history/`.
